een as we've been able  to use schemes like the furlough  scheming which has been an absolute  lifeline that a lot of us are having to  go down the route of very difficult  decisions in applying for quite  significant loans and that's not helped  by the fact that even though the Bank of  England has cut rates to just not 0.1%  banks aren't all passing that on to  customers so will this governor do what  Mark Carney ruled out and maybe even cut  rates into negative territory  I think previous people on the MPC and  previous governments would say they  didn't they didn't have in mind the  scenario that we're in today and I think  it's wise not to rule anything off the  table unlikely as it is it's striking  that unprecedented remedies are on the  table and with the UK facing an  unprecedented collapse in the economic  activity with banks being asked to  provide unprecedented support who can  rule anything out  Eddie Conway Sky News
 

